# Vulnerability details

## Impact
When users take a flash loan, an amount is sent to the receiver, and then some action takes place, after that action that sent amount is expected to be paid + some fee. Users can also call `PositionAction::decreaseLever` through a proxy, to "Decrease the leverage of a position by taking out a credit flash loan to withdraw and sell collateral", after it is called, the flash loan lender sends the credit and calls `onCreditFlashLoan`, which handles all that logic.

However, at the end of `onCreditFlashLoan`, the protocol is approving the flash lender of an amount `subDebt` which doesn't include the fees, it is also not handled when subtracting the debt from the corresponding position.

When fees are >0, `PositionAction::decreaseLever` will always revert as the protocol will always revert with `ERC20: insufficient allowance`, as `Flashlender::creditFlashLoan` will try to transfer amount + fees, which is not approved on the other side.

