As seen in the code, there is no check if the `token ==
address(ICDPVault(vault).token())`, which means that a user can create a Permit2 signature for literally every token and the deposit will go through. For example if a user deposit 1 DAI (worth 1$ and has 18 decimals) he will be able to steal 1 Ether from the Ethereum stored in `PositionAction` and then immediately withdrawing it by simply calling `CDPVault::withdraw()` function.

