## Impact
The unspent asset might not be able to return its owner

## Proof of Concept
A user can deposit collateral for a  position by delegate-calling `PositionAction#deposit()` though its `userProxy`. 
If the caller doesn't have collateral at the moment, they can provide a `collateralParams.auxSwap` parameter to swap `targetToken` for collateral, then deposit the received collateral into the designated position.

If the value of `collateralParams.auxSwap.swapType` is `SwapType.EXACT_IN`, `collateralParams.auxSwap.amount` is used to specify how many `targetToken` the caller is willing to spend to for swapping collateral.
Otherwise, `collateralParams.auxSwap.amount` is used to specify how many collateral the caller is willing to get through swapping:
