# Vulnerability details

## Impact
`PositionAction#decreaseLever()` fails to work due to insufficient assets and allowance for the flash loan repayment. As a result, anyone who increases the leverage of their position has no way to decrease it by calling `PositionAction#decreaseLever()`, putting them at high risk of being liquidated.

## Proof of Concept
A user who increased the leverage of their position should be able to decrease their leverage  by calling `PositionAction#decreaseLever()`. a specific amount of `WETH` will be borrowed from `flashlender` to repay user's position, then the collateral can be withdrawn from the position and swap to `WETH` to repay the flash loan.
The amount of flash loan repayment is calculated in `Flashlender#creditFlashLoan()`:
```solidity
    function creditFlashLoan(
        ICreditFlashBorrower receiver,
        uint256 amount,
        bytes calldata data
    ) external override nonReentrant returns (bool) {
        uint256 fee = wmul(amount, protocolFee);
@>      uint256 total = amount + fee; //@audit-info total flash loan repayment

        pool.lendCreditAccount(amount, address(receiver));

        emit CreditFlashLoan(address(receiver), amount, fee);

        if (receiver.onCreditFlashLoan(msg.sender, amount, fee, data) != CALLBACK_SUCCESS_CREDIT)
            revert Flash__creditFlashLoan_callbackFailed();

        // reverts if not enough Stablecoin have been send back
@>      underlyingToken.transferFrom(address(receiver), address(pool), total);//@audit-info force receiver to repay flash loan
        pool.repayCreditAccount(total - fee, fee, 0);

        return true;
    }
```
However, the receiver doesn't provide sufficient asset for flash loan repayment, the flash loan fee was not accounted in `subDebt`:
