```

This function helps with updating the `currentPrice` price and this price is used in the larger Loopfi ecosystem.

Issue here however is the fact that there is a [hardcoded implementation](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-07-loopfi/blob/57871f64bdea450c1f04c9a53dc1a78223719164/src/oracle/BalancerOracle.sol#L121-L122) of `totalSupply()` in order to get the pool's total supply.

But this would be inaccurate with some pools.
getActualSupply() should be used instead

According to [Balancer's docs](https://docs.balancer.fi/concepts/advanced/valuing-bpt/valuing-bpt.html#getting-bpt-supply) on getting bpt supply, this is not the way to do it for all the vaults _(i.e totalSupply())_ and it should only be used for old "legacy" pools.

To quote the docs:

> [!NOTE]
> Don't use `totalSupply` without reading this first!
> Balancer Pools with pre-minted BPT will always return type(uint211).max.
> There are three potential functions to query when determining the BPT supply depending on pool type. When evaluating a new pool type, ensure that you are using the correct supply function!
> getActualSupply
> This is the most common/current function to call. getActualSupply is used by the most recent versions of Weighted and Stable Pools. It accounts for pre-minted BPT as well as due protocol fees.

More can be read on [here](https://docs.balancer.fi/concepts/advanced/valuing-bpt/valuing-bpt.html#getactualsupply), but as seen, `getActualSupply` should be used instead because it accounts for pre-minted BPT as well as due protocol fees. but in our case [here](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-07-loopfi/blob/57871f64bdea450c1f04c9a53dc1a78223719164/src/oracle/BalancerOracle.sol#L121), only `totalSupply()` is used which means that the wrong price would be used for the pool, since this is the [final step](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-07-loopfi/blob/57871f64bdea450c1f04c9a53dc1a78223719164/src/oracle/BalancerOracle.sol#L136) on how the currentPrice would be achieved `currentPrice = wdiv(wmul(totalPi, IWeightedPool(pool).getInvariant()), totalSupply);`.

## Impact

Using `totalSupply()` instead of `getActualSupply()` for newer Balancer pools would lead to storing/ingesting incorrect prices, as it doesn't account for pre-minted BPT and fees, essentially making our expected safe prices unsafe.

