            address(this),
            address(this),
            0,
            -toInt256(creditParams.amount)
        );
    }
```
## Impact
Users can craft malicious swap pathways that may falsely deposit a big amount of collateral.
The pool doesn't accept multiple tokens as collateral, depositing collateral based on a different token's amount is unfair to all other users.
Users may create pools made up of the targetToken + malicious tokens and intentionally make the exchange rate very extreme in order to make the contract behave as if a lot of collateral has been deposited. This can dilute the collateral earnings for all other fair-behaving depositors.
## Tools Used
Manual review
## Recommended Mitigation Steps
Make sure the last path of the swap action results in the targetToken, otherwise arbitrary tokens can be utilized to generate the amount of collateral that will be deposited.


